## Additional permission

In addition to what the PolyForm Strict License 1.0.0 allows, Aprilox gives you
permission to use unmodified copies of the software for commercial purposes, as
long as both of these are true:

1. The use is free of charge: nobody pays you, and you charge nobody, for the
   software, for access to it or for its use (for example as a hosted or
   managed service, or as part of a paid offer).
2. What you create with the software (code, applications, games, documents or
   any other result) is not intended to be sold, rented or provided for a fee,
   including work done for a paying client.

Aprilox also gives you permission to keep the files the software writes into
your projects (such as its guides in .athanor/) in those projects, and to share
or publish them unchanged with those projects, but not to use them apart from
those projects.

These permissions do not allow you to change the software, to make new works
based on it or to distribute it otherwise, and they end together with your
other licenses under these terms.

## Attribution

Every project you create or change with the software must say so:

1. in the project's README (or, without one, its main documentation), this line:
   Made with Athanor (https://github.com/Aprilox/Athanor), created by Aprilox.
2. at the root of its source code, a file named NOTICE that contains the same
   line.

Keep these mentions in every copy and every version of the project that you
share or publish, and do not remove them or make them hard to see.

## Asking for permission

Anything these terms do not allow (changing the software, using any part of its
source code in another work, sharing or distributing it, any commercial use
beyond the additional permission above) needs Aprilox's written permission
beforehand. Ask for it by opening an issue on https://github.com/Aprilox/Athanor.
A permission counts only when Aprilox gives it in writing, and only for what it
says.

Selling or distributing the software, or any work based on it, for a fee, and
using its source code to build a third-party tool, product or service offered
for a fee, are reserved to Aprilox.

## Third-party components

Parts of Athanor that come from third parties keep their own licenses (listed in
the README's Acknowledgements, their texts next to them); these terms do not
reduce the rights those licenses give for those parts.

## Earlier versions

Versions up to and including 2.51.0 were first published under the MIT License.
Since version 2.51.1 was published, Aprilox offers every version of Athanor,
those included, only under these terms, and no longer under the MIT License.
